  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With `n` `points` on a 2D plane where `points[i] = [xi, yi]`, Output*the **widest vertical area** between two points such that no points are inside the area.*\n\nA **vertical area** is an area of fixed-width extending infinitely along the y-axis (i.e., infinite height). The **widest vertical area** is the one with the largest width.\n\nKeep in mind that points **on the edge** of a vertical area **are not** considered included in the area.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n![](https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/09/19/points3.png)​\n\n```\nInput: points = [[8,7],[9,9],[7,4],[9,7]]\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: Both the red and the blue area are optimal.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: points = [[3,1],[9,0],[1,0],[1,4],[5,3],[8,8]]\nOutput: 3\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `n == points.length`\n* `2 <= n <= 105`\n* `points[i].length == 2`\n* `0 <= xi, yi <= 109`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
